Coverage (JadeOx, 2026-10-03). There's one JSON Schema per identifier the code emits on HEAD e9b729e. That's 11 identifiers: the five the bead names plus the six added since.

- `keyval.dev.error/v1`, `keyval.dev.doctor/v2`, `keyval.dev.check/v1`, `keyval.dev.gate/v3`, `keyval.dev.receipt/v3` (the gate receipt);
- `keyval.dev.accept/v1`, `keyval.dev.commit/v1`, `keyval.dev.close/v1`, `keyval.dev.beads-import/v1`, `keyval.dev.prune/v1`, and `keyval.dev.step/v1` (the W01.6 step records).

Files: `schemas/dev/<name>.v<n>.schema.json` (draft 2020-12, closed, every field required, `schema` const), `schemas/dev/invalid/<name>.v<n>.json` (one negative fixture each, naming the rule it breaks and the JSON pointer where it must be rejected), and `schemas/dev/README.md`.

Check DEV-SCHEMAS (`xtask/src/check.rs`, T0, covers O-6, min_cases 18) selects `schemas::`:
- `xtask/src/schemas.rs` (14 cases):
  - Catalogue: every identifier literal in xtask/src has a schema and a negative fixture, and there are no orphans.
  - Schema shape: each schema is closed and names its identifier.
  - Negative fixtures: each one is rejected at its pointer.
  - Enums: every serialised enum variant equals its schema's `enum` (an exhaustive list, so a new variant fails).
  - Real outputs, from each command's own code:
    - error_json for every kind;
    - doctor::run reaching all four tool statuses;
    - check::run reaching all four check statuses;
    - gate::run (static steps on the gate-ok fixture) for the report, the receipt file and steps.jsonl, both verdicts;
    - commit::run on a scratch repo, all three outcomes plus the receipt files;
    - a close report embedding a real commit report;
    - accept::run (labels selection, plus an early refusal);
    - beads::run --dry-run with stand-in trackers;
    - prune::run on a scratch layout, dry and real;
    - StepLog::record, passed and failed.
- `xtask/tests/schemas.rs` (4 cases): the binary's stdout for `--json nope`, `gate integration --json` (not_implemented), `check AGENTS-RULES --json`, `check NOPE AGENTS-RULES --json`, and `doctor --json`.

Evidence so far, in a private copy of e9b729e plus these paths:
- `./dev check DEV-SCHEMAS`: passed, 18 cases (min 18).
- DEV-CHECK: passed, 13 cases.
- clippy -D warnings and fmt: clean.
- Schema-drift mutants, all killed:
  - a renamed CommitReport field fails 1 of 18;
  - prune's SCHEMA bumped to v2 with no schema fails 13 of 18;
  - a new prune Reason variant fails to compile in the exhaustive list.
- The Python jsonschema 4.19 cross-check validated all 601 current-version artifacts in artifacts/receipts (17 accept, 28 commit, 1 prune, 35 receipt/v3, 520 step records), plus six live `./dev --json` outputs. Older receipt/v1, v2 and bootstrap-receipt/v0 files predate these schemas and are not covered.

The commit also brings AGENTS.md's `./dev check` list up to the catalogue (adding DEV-SCHEMAS, NEWTYPES, KEY-VALUE, DOMAIN-ENUMS, ERROR-CODES and PORTS), and adds one sentence pointing at schemas/dev. Acceptance is the `accept:DEV-SCHEMAS` label.

SunnyDog — W04.4 design (W04's LAST subtask: its commit carries `Bead: br-w04-domain-types-ports-bv5`, so W04 closes through the wrapper):
- Compile-fail fixtures live in the existing lint-probe-deterministic crate (it depends on types and is a workspace member), so no manifest or lock change. There are 10 cfg-gated modules, each forging a types value from outside the crate:
  - forge_key, forge_value, forge_node_id, forge_version (a CAS expecting version 0), forge_page_size: E0423 (private tuple fields);
  - forge_terminal_result (index 0) and forge_scan_range (inverted): E0451 (private fields);
  - version_vs_index (CD-4): E0308;
  - submitted_with_result (an attempt both submitted and terminal, CD-2): E0618;
  - ready_and_failed (a lifecycle with a flag, CD-2): E0559.
  Each code was confirmed by compiling the fixture. The control build (the existing controls_pass_the_full_policy) compiles, so passes are not vacuous.
- Harness: lint::probes::compile_fail, 10 tests reusing LINT-PROBES' assert_rejected (JSON diagnostics, step-logged, rerunnable with ./dev check COMPILE-FAIL or LINT-PROBES --case <name>).
- Already proven by W01.3, and cited rather than duplicated (all under the deterministic configuration that LINT-TIERS proves types carries byte for byte): wildcard_arm and binding_catch_all_arm (CD-5, both arm kinds), missing_docs (CD-11), and disallowed (Instant::now and every other determinism entry).
- DEP-RULE's failing fixture already exists (tiers::tests::a_deterministic_crate_depending_on_an_adapter_is_rejected). The new narrow check DEP-RULE-FIXTURES (tiers::tests::, min 9) selects it plus the other forbidden-edge fixtures.
- Registry: COMPILE-FAIL (CD-2, CD-3, CD-4; min 10) and DEP-RULE-FIXTURES (CD-1, T-12; min 9) go in the check.rs bootstrap catalogue. W04's accept gains COMPILE-FAIL, DEP-RULE-FIXTURES and LINT-PROBES.
- READING: W04's acceptance says "registered in registry/checks.toml", but that file is W05.1's and does not exist yet. The check.rs CATALOGUE is the bootstrap registry ("W05 can move the rows across unchanged", check.rs doc), so all W04 checks (NEWTYPES, KEY-VALUE, DOMAIN-ENUMS, ERROR-CODES, PORTS, COMPILE-FAIL, DEP-RULE-FIXTURES) are registered there with markers and selectors.
